[Link to tutorial](https://rpubs.com/alecri/258589)

## Prerequisites

```{r load_libs}
if (!require(pacman)) install.packages("pacman")
pacman::p_load(tidyverse, plotly, shiny, scales, patchwork, DiagrammeR,
               survival, KMsurv, flexsurv, eha, ctqr, cmprsk, mstate, ggsurvfit, survminer, 
               Epi, epitools, gnm, splines)
```

```{r set_theme}
theme_set(theme_classic() + theme(legend.position = "bottom"))
```

## Data

```{r data}
orca <- read.table("http://www.stats4life.se/data/oralca.txt", stringsAsFactors = TRUE)
head(orca)
glimpse(orca)
summary(orca)
table(orca$event)
```

## Survival Data

```{r death}
orca |> 
    mutate(all = event != "Alive") -> orca
table(orca$all)
```

Defining a `Surv` object needs a $(y, \delta)$ pair
```{r surv_obj}
su_obj <- Surv(orca$time, orca$all)
str(su_obj)
```

## Estimating Survival Function

### Non Parametric

#### KM Estimator

```{r km}
fit_km <- survfit(Surv(time, all) ~ 1, data = orca)
print(fit_km)
```

Tidy data

```{r km_tidy}
tidy(fit_km) |> View()
```

Visualize

```{r hm_viz}
ggsurvfit(fit_km) +
    add_censor_mark()+
      add_confidence_interval() +
  add_risktable() +
  labs(x = "Time (years)")
```

CIF & Cumulative Hazard

```{r km_cif_ch}
ggsurvfit(fit_km, type = "risk")
ggsurvfit(fit_km, type = "cumhaz")
```
